To run examples in the OSCAR framework, follow these steps:

First, source the external libraries by running the following command: source /software/STCF/OSCAR/ExternalLibs-gcc85/bashrc.sh

Next, you will need an OSCAR offline package. You can copy one from my home directory: /home/bbq/offline. After copying, delete the build and install directories, rebuild the program, and then source the setup file: offline/install/setup.sh

Alternatively, you can also download the offline package from GitLab at https://git.ustc.edu.cn/. If you choose this option, please create a GitLab account first. Once your account is set up, let me know, and I will invite you to join the OSCAR/offline project. 


After completing the setup, you can explore some example scripts located in the following directory: $OFFLINETOP/Examples

Here are a couple of useful scripts:

$OFFLINETOP/Examples/RunCheck/sim_particleGun.py — for simulating all the STCF detectors.

$OFFLINETOP/Examples/RunCheck/rec_Full.py — for digitization and reconstruction of all detectors.


Please note that all algorithms in the offline framework are written in C/C++ and are executed by configuring Python scripts. This includes setting up the geometry (using DD4hep), event data model (based on Podio), Geant4-based simulation, digitization, and reconstruction et al.

If you have any questions or run into any issues, feel free to contact me.

