---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

OSCAR manages detector simulation with a Task，which consists of Algorithms and services:
- A dedicated algorithm (DetSimAlg) for all sub-detectors simulation
- A dedicated service (G4Svc) for launching Geant4 within OSCAR
- A user-end service(DetSimFactory) to set up and organize all the Geant4 related classes.
- A user-end service(AnalysisElement) for access to G4Event to create EDM


- AnalysisElement
A DetSimAlg can contains many different AnaMgrs inherit from AnalysisElement. These AnaMgrs implement different functions.
For example, GeneratorMgr - for generating event, GeoAnaMgr - for storing geometry in root file, and MDCAnaMgr - for getting information from MDC detector simutation. Other sub-detectors
can also have their own AnaMgr to get simulation truth information.


The work flow of the FullSim is :

1. The geometry model is initialized by the GeometrySvc and constructed in
Geant4. Note that both xml and gdml format of the geometry compact file are
supported for geometry construction. Sometimes one wants to use the
DetectorConstruction.hh in geant4 to initialize a detector, he/she can choose
whether to use the GeometrySvc to initialize the detector by a property
GeometrySvcEnable:
```python
import GeometrySvc
myxmlsvc = task.createSvc("GeometrySvc")
myxmlsvc.property("GeoCompactFileName").set("Geometry/compact/STCF.xml")
```
2. Detector response is simulated in the Geant4-based Detector simulation module.
3. The GeoAnaMgr obtain the detector geometry from the memory and
save it into a root file as TGeo format . the DetAnaMgr obtain the MC events from
the memory and save them into a root file in TTree .


## GeometrySvc
GeometrySvc is a user-end service for parsing detector geometry compact
description file and construct detector model in memory with all the necessary
data stored in a detector geometry compact file. When users want to do some
simulation work in an Oscar detector simulation algorithm package，the first thing
he or she has to do is initial and construct a detector model from the detector
compact description file(such as a xml or gdml file)by using the
GeometrySvc. The picture shows how to use it ,you need to modify the run.py
script.
1. Create and import the GeometrySvc.
2. Set the GeometrySvc enable to true.
3. Set the GeoCmpactFileName according to the rule in the example.


